    feat(wifi): port BK7258 STA networking to OpenVela

    Add the AP-owned BK7258 Wi-Fi transport and controller contract used by the OpenVela netdev.

    - Add fixed-width scan-page and country IPC commands with static ABI checks.

    - Keep radio, WPA, association, EAPOL, and PHY ownership in Armino while forwarding STA ARP/IPv4 to OpenVela.

    - Add scan completion handling and a stable multi-page scan result snapshot.

    - Harden direct-push pbuf ownership and return definite mailbox enqueue failures to the AP.

    - Include the mailbox RX backpressure, ACK, reset, and poll dependencies required by the tested transport.

    - Reserve the 16 MiB PSRAM layout used by the final app_ab build.

    Validated with a clean BK7258 app_ab build and on-board scan success.

